# Beacon UI (bento dark, preferred styling)

All Compose UI in Beacon follows this design system (TSI-inspired bento dark). Do not introduce ad-hoc colors, tiny touch targets, or dense layouts.

## Principles

- **Accessibility first**: visually impaired users are the primary audience. The dark
  near-black background with bold lime/yellow/white tiles is deliberately high-contrast.
- **Bento layout**: bold colored cards/tiles, large radii, one big primary tile per screen.
- **Calm companion**: simple, reassuring copy; keep guidance text short.
- **High contrast**: strong foreground/background separation; never gray-on-gray.

## Use the design system

- Theme: `BeaconTheme` in `ui/theme/Theme.kt` (single dark scheme, `BentoDarkColors`)
- Tokens: `BeaconDimens`, `BeaconShapes`, colors in `Color.kt`, `BeaconTypography` in `Type.kt`
- Scaffold: `BeaconScreen` (dark, scrollable) + `BeaconTopBar` (wordmark + circular action) + `BeaconHeading`
- Bento tiles: `BentoCard` (title, optional value/leadingIcon, arrow-circle) — whole tile is one tap target
- Chips/status pills: `BeaconChip` (selected = white or accent fill)
- Flow actions: `BigActionButton` (primary), `SecondaryActionButton` (outlined)
- Status blocks: `BeaconStatusCard`
- Emergency: a `BentoCard` (or `BigActionButton`) with `containerColor = BeaconDanger` — always red, always reachable

## Colors (Color.kt)

- Background: `BeaconBackground` (#0A0A0A); dark tiles: `BeaconCardDark`
- Lime tile (primary action): `BeaconLime` / text `BeaconLimeText`
- Yellow tile: `BeaconYellow` / text `BeaconYellowText`
- White tile: `BeaconWhiteCard` / text `BeaconWhiteCardText`
- Emergency: `BeaconDanger` / text `BeaconDangerText`
- Text on dark: `BeaconOnDark`, muted `BeaconOnDarkMuted`
- Do not add custom colors outside `Color.kt`.

## Touch targets

- Primary buttons / large tiles: min `BeaconDimens.primaryButtonMinHeight` / `bentoLargeMinHeight`
- Small bento tiles: min `bentoSmallMinHeight`; wide tiles: `bentoWideMinHeight`
- Never use controls smaller than 48dp; arrow circles are `arrowCircle` (44dp)

## Typography (bold geometric)

- Page title: `displaySmall`; tile title: `headlineSmall`; big numbers/values: `displaySmall`
- Body: `bodyLarge` / `bodyMedium`; chips: `titleMedium`
- Do not shrink essential text below `bodyMedium`

## TalkBack

- Every interactive control needs a clear `contentDescription` (use the component params).
- Interactive containers (`BentoCard`, `BigActionButton`, `SecondaryActionButton`, top-bar
  action, device cards) use `clearAndSetSemantics` so the whole tile reads as one node. When
  doing this on a clickable, you MUST also set `role = Role.Button` and re-add the action with
  `onClick(action = { ...; true })` (clearing semantics drops the clickable's action), and call
  `disabled()` when not enabled. Otherwise TalkBack won't activate it on double-tap.
- Toggles: make the whole row `Modifier.toggleable(value, role = Role.Switch, onValueChange)`
  and set the inner `Switch(onCheckedChange = null)` so label + state are one announced control.
- Decorative visuals (Canvas illustrations, background icons) must be hidden from TalkBack:
  `Modifier.clearAndSetSemantics {}`, and decorative `Icon`/`Image` use `contentDescription = null`.
- Use `liveRegion = LiveRegionMode.Polite` for connection/battery/error status and for content
  that changes in place (e.g. onboarding pages, recognised voice text).
- Page/section titles use `Modifier.semantics { heading() }` (already in `BeaconHeading`/`BeaconTopBar`).
- No business logic in Composables; use ViewModels + sealed UI state.

## What to avoid

- Light backgrounds or low-contrast gray tiles
- Tiny icon-only buttons without descriptions
- Long paragraphs on guidance screens
- Requesting all permissions at once without education copy
